{
  "dom_id": "step-q100703",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the solution of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12)=4.$",
  "worked_solution": "The logarithms share the same base, and so we can combine them using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12) & =4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{12}) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x/12)} & ={e}^{4} \\\\ \\frac{x}{12} & ={e}^{4} \\\\ x & =12{e}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
